{
 "$comment": "The copy gates. Two lists of regular expressions that refuse filler in outward copy. The noise list catches performed sincerity, narrated answers and product filler. The prose list catches captions in place of sentences, money figures with no payer, metaphors for the product, labels in place of sentences and modifier tails on names. A pattern may carry `requires` and `unless`, case-sensitive expressions tested against the sentence around the hit, and `min_words`. Noise patterns match case-insensitively. Prose patterns run after URLs are replaced by <url>.",
 "families": {
  "performed-sincerity": "a phrase announcing that the writer is being honest instead of being honest",
  "narrating-the-answer": "a phrase that describes the sentence that follows instead of saying it",
  "filler-noise": "marketing filler that would fit any product",
  "caption-for-a-link": "a noun phrase ending in a colon in front of a link, in place of a sentence that says what the link is",
  "figure-without-payer": "a percent or money figure with no clause saying who pays or gets it",
  "product-metaphor": "a metaphor or coined name standing in for the product or its output",
  "label-not-sentence": "a noun phrase ending in a colon alone on a line, followed by prose instead of a list",
  "modifier-tail": "a name with a relative clause or a participial phrase hung off it instead of the plain noun"
 },
